uested 500mg vs candidate specifies 1000mg or\n<truncated 1696 bytes>\nid JSON object matching this schema:\r\n45: {\r\n46:   \"results\": [\r\n47:     {\r\n48:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\r\n49:       \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\" | \"no_match\",\r\n50:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID, or empty string if no_match)\",\r\n51:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation for review/no_match, empty string for match)\"\r\n52:     }\r\n53:   ]\r\n54: }\r\n55: \r\n56: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\r\n57: - MANDATORY: You MUST return a result item for EVERY SINGLE input case_id. If the input contains N cases, \"results\" MUST contain exactly N items.\r\n58: - NEVER omit any case_id under any circumstances!\r\n59: - For each case_id:\r\n60:   * \"status\": \"match\" (if there is a valid match, specify candidate item_id, empty reason)\r\n61:   * \"status\": \"review\" (if same drug & strength but different dosage form, specify candidate item_id and Arabic reason)\r\n62:   * \"status\": \"no_match\" (if strength conflict, generic alternative, different brand, or no valid match; item_id is \"\", with Arabic reason)\r\n63: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\r\n64: \"\"\"\r\n65: \r\n66: def norm_num(s: str) -> str:\r\n67:     s = str(s)\r\n68:     for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩', '0123456789'):\r\n69:         s = s.replace(e, w)\r\n70:     return s\r\n71: \r\n72: def get_strength_pattern(text: str) -> str | None:\r\n73:     text = norm_num(text.lower())\r\n74:     m = re.search(r'(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(مجم|مج|جم|جرام|gm|mg|mcg|مكجم)', text)\r\n75:     if m:\r\n76:         val = m.group(1)\r\n77:         unit = m.group(2)\r\n78:         if unit in ['جم', 'جرام', 'gm']:\r\n79:             # Pharmacological rule: tablets/capsules/pills never come in multi-gram dosages (>=5g).\r\n80:             # In Egyptian warehouse price lists, '10 جم اقراص' is a common shorthand for 10 mg (not 10,000 mg!).\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
